# Commit Message Guidelines

## Pattern
- Start with a verb in present tense
- Keep first line under 50 characters
- Focus on what changed and why

## Examples
✅ Good:
- "Add user authentication"
- "Fix navigation menu on mobile"
- "Update README with setup instructions"
- "Remove deprecated API endpoints"

❌ Avoid:
- "For user auth, adding login"
- "Fixed the thing"
- "Updates"
- "For mobile, fixing nav"

## Rules
1. Use present tense verbs:
   - Add
   - Update
   - Fix
   - Remove
   - Refactor
   - Improve
   - Change

2. Be specific about the change
3. Include the component/file affected if relevant
4. Add more details in the body if needed